        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ui): explain replace-mode filtering in model picker",
        "body": "Closes #104545\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen `models.mode: \"replace\"` filters the model catalog, the Control UI showed the resulting models without explaining why other bundled or discovered models might be absent.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nConfigured model-list responses now carry additive `catalogMode: \"replace\"` metadata. The chat model picker and Quick Settings use that metadata to explain that model settings are filtering the catalog, without claiming that every visible row was explicitly configured. Full-catalog (`view: \"all\"`) responses do not carry the hint metadata.\n\nThe picker action opens the Models section directly at `/settings/ai-agents?section=models#config-section-models`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can tell that local model settings are filtering the catalog and can navigate directly to the relevant settings instead of treating an absent model as an upstream support problem.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Rebased onto `main` at `017217bae33e`; exact pushed head: `596bddb4fb4f`.\n- The final history preserves current main's chat session-projection behavior and this PR's replace-mode hint/navigation behavior.\n- Current `ui/AGENTS.md` contributor policy is followed: the PR includes the English source change and required raw-copy baseline only. Generated fallback metadata and non-English locale bundles are absent from the diff and remain owned by the locale refresh workflow.\n- The exact local `scripts/ci-changed-scope.mjs` preflight passed with the PR's real branch/base/head inputs.\n- Focused Gateway regressions: 2 files, 48 tests passed.\n  - `pnpm exec vitest run --config test/vitest/vitest.gateway.config.ts src/gateway/server-methods/models.test.ts`\n- Focused Control UI regressions: 5 files, 265 tests passed.\n  - `pnpm --dir ui exec vitest run --config vitest.config.ts src/pages/chat/chat-state.test.ts src/pages/chat/chat-view.test.ts src/pages/chat/models.test.ts src/pages/config/quick.test.ts src/pages/model-providers/data.test.ts`\n- Targeted Chromium replace-mode regression: 1 passed, 6 skipped.\n  - `pnpm exec vitest run --config test/vitest/vitest.ui-e2e.config.ts --configLoader runner ui/src/e2e/chat-composer-redesign.e2e.test.ts -t 'explains model filtering in replace mode'`\n- `pnpm protocol:check` passed with generated TypeScript, Swift, and Kotlin outputs stable.\n- `pnpm ui:i18n:verify` passed under the contributor workflow.\n- `pnpm lint --threads=8` passed.\n- Repository-wide `pnpm format:check` passed across 23,055 files; focused changed-file `oxfmt --check` also passed.\n- `pnpm check:max-lines-ratchet`, `pnpm deadcode:unused-files`, and `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD` passed.\n- Desktop 1280x900 and mobile 393x852 proof remains in the earlier immutable proof comment. The rebased implementation preserves the same visible hint and Manage models navigation behavior.\n\nBefore: the UI silently presented the filtered catalog.\n\nAfter: the picker and Quick Settings state, \"Replace mode filters models according to your model settings,\" and link directly to the Models settings section.\n\nAI-assisted: Codex was used to implement, test, and review this change. No agent transcript is attached.\n",
        "branch": "agent/model-picker-replace-mode-hint",
